<% content_for :title, "Corpus analysis — NavishAI" %>
<main class="page-shell">
  <%= link_to @corpus.name, workspace_corpus_path(Current.workspace, @corpus), class: "back-link" %>
  <div class="page-heading"><div><h1>Corpus analysis</h1><p><%= @analysis.model? && @model_result ? "#{@model_result.fetch('decision').humanize} · attempt complete" : @analysis.state.humanize %> · <%= @analysis.processing_method %></p></div><%= link_to "Refresh result", workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis, family_focus: @family_focus, page: @page), class: "button" %></div>
  <% if @analysis_input_error %>
    <p role="alert" class="inline-error"><%= @analysis_input_error %></p>
    <p>This fixed analysis has not changed. No partial source preview or candidates are shown. <%= link_to "Return to the corpus", workspace_corpus_path(Current.workspace, @corpus) %> to inspect sources<%= @analysis.large? ? "." : " or prepare smaller inputs and request a new analysis." %></p>
    <% if @analysis.large? && @analysis.state == "complete" %>
      <p>Only this evidence preview is blocked. Explore fixed families within their page bounds; narrow a source signal filter if needed. No new analysis or disclosure is required.</p>
      <ul id="bounded-family-links" role="list"><% @clusters.each do |cluster| %><li><%= link_to cluster.label, workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_issue_cluster_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis, cluster) %></li><% end %></ul>
      <%= render "shared/record_pagination", more: @more, page_number: @page %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif @analysis.model? %>
    <p>Model-proposed issue families and scenarios from your fixed source records. Exact quotes prove source links, not correct classification or expectations. No expert label or scenario approval comes from this analysis.</p>
    <% if @analysis.stale? %><p role="status">Company documentation changed after this request. Inspect the fixed history here; review current evidence before compiling scenarios.</p><% end %>
    <details><summary>Fixed model settings and attempt</summary><pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@analysis.configuration.merge("request_key" => @analysis.request_key, "input_digest" => @analysis.input_digest)) %></pre></details>
    <details><summary>Disclosed source records</summary><pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@model_input) %></pre></details>
    <% if @analysis.batch? %>
      <h2>Batch progress and receipts</h2><p>Maximum <%= @analysis.call_plan.fetch("maximum_calls") %> once-only calls to the fixed endpoint/model/settings. Retained batch proposals are not partial global families or approved scenarios.</p>
      <p>Discovery digests bind exact records. The reducer definition binds ordered batch UUIDs and their input digests; its receipt also records the exact derived proposal-input digest. Full membership quotes remain local; the reducer receives one exact representative quote per cluster and all candidate definitions/evidence.</p>
      <details><summary>Frozen allocation and call plan</summary><pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@analysis.call_plan) %></pre></details>
      <% @analysis.corpus_discovery_batches.order(:position).each do |batch| %>
        <details class="source-record"><summary><%= batch.phase.humanize %> <%= batch.position %> · <%= batch.state == "queued" && @analysis.state.in?(%w[complete failed]) ? "Not sent — attempt stopped" : batch.state.humanize %></summary>
          <pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(batch.attributes.slice("request_key", "input_refs", "input_digest", "started_at", "finished_at", "result")) %></pre>
        </details>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <% if @model_result %>
      <h2><%= @model_result.fetch("decision").humanize %></h2><p><%= @model_result.fetch("reason") %></p>
      <details><summary>Fixed model response and reported cost</summary><p>Missing usage/cost stays unknown. Endpoint reports are not verified charges or quality evidence.<% if @analysis.batch? %> This response reports only the final call, not the total. Inspect each batch receipt for its own reported usage/cost; unknown reports prevent a known total.<% end %></p><pre class="evidence-text"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@model_result) %></pre></details>
      <% if @model_result["schema"] == BatchCorpusDiscovery::GLOBAL_RELATIONSHIPS_VERSION %>
        <section class="section-block" id="support-relationships" aria-labelledby="support-relationships-title">
          <h2 id="support-relationships-title">Cross-batch support relationships</h2>
          <p>New proposals from fixed observation anchors in separate batches, not expert truth. Every quote comes from an original observation retained below. Missing evidence, account scope, chronology and causality need expert review; this is not exhaustive corpus understanding.</p>
          <% if @model_result.fetch("relationships").empty? %><p role="status">No cross-batch relationships proposed. This does not establish that no contradiction or support issue exists; one discovery batch cannot supply a cross-batch relationship.</p><% end %>
          <% @model_result.fetch("relationships").each do |relationship| %><%= render "support_finding", finding: relationship %><% end %>
        </section>
      <% elsif @analysis.relationships? %><p role="status">No global support relationships published. Intermediate receipts are not partial global findings.</p><% end %>
      <% if @model_result["schema"].in?([ ModelCorpusDiscovery::OBSERVATIONS_VERSION, BatchCorpusDiscovery::GLOBAL_RELATIONSHIPS_VERSION ]) %>
        <section class="section-block" id="support-observations" aria-labelledby="support-observations-title">
          <h2 id="support-observations-title">Source-backed support observations</h2>
          <p>Proposals, not verified findings or expert decisions. Every anchor links the fixed source disclosed for this attempt. Candidate selection does not remove observations; quotes do not prove a diagnosis, resolution or correct policy.</p>
          <% if @analysis.relationships? %><p>All original observations remain unchanged, independent of new relationships or selected candidates.</p>
          <% elsif @analysis.batch? %><p>The reducer preserves existing findings; it cannot create new relationships across batches.</p><% end %>
          <% if @model_result.fetch("observations").empty? %><p role="status">No observations retained. This does not establish that no support issue exists.</p><% end %>
          <% @model_result.fetch("observations").each do |observation| %><%= render "support_finding", finding: observation %><% end %>
        </section>
      <% elsif @analysis.observations? %><p role="status">No global support observations published. Any retained batch proposal remains an intermediate receipt, not a partial global finding.</p>
      <% else %><p>This v1 protocol did not request support observations. Missing findings do not establish that no support issue exists.</p><% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <p>Local term clustering, not semantic diagnosis. It uses titles and <%= @analysis.full_text? ? "the complete text" : "the first 4000 characters" %> of each conversation, with a 0.3 cosine threshold. Labels come from your corpus, not a fixed taxonomy. Keyword mentions do not prove failures or risk.</p>
    <% if @analysis.large? || @analysis.full_text? %><p><%= @analysis.large_full_text? ? "Large full-text local limits: 100,000 complete records / 1 GiB" : (@analysis.full_text? ? "Full-text local limits: 2000 complete records / 10 MiB" : "Streaming local limits: 100,000 complete records / 1 GiB") %>, 2 million conversation-term entries, 250,000 distinct terms and 2 million seed comparisons. A budget failure retains no proposals and never retries automatically. Complete evidence reads remain bounded to 10 MiB. These bounds do not grant model disclosure or prove discovery quality.</p><% end %>
  <% end %>
  <% if @analysis.state == "failed" %><p role="alert" class="inline-error"><%= @analysis.error %></p><% end %>
  <% if @analysis.state.in?(%w[queued running]) %>
    <% unless @analysis_input_error %><p role="status"><%= @analysis.batch? ? "Fixed batches execute in order, followed by at most one reducer. Refresh sends nothing. Errors and interruptions block later calls; no automatic retry or continuation." : (@analysis.model? ? "One fixed model attempt; it may send the disclosed records to the approved endpoint. No automatic retry." : "Waiting for the local processing job. No data leaves this deployment.") %></p><% end %>
    <% if Current.require_membership!.can_write? && (@analysis.batch? || @analysis.state == "queued" || @analysis.started_at < 10.minutes.ago) %><%= button_to "Interrupt analysis attempt", interrupt_workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis), class: "button" %><% end %>
  <% end %>
  <% if @analysis.state == "complete" && !@analysis_input_error %>
    <p><%= pluralize(@analysis.summary["selected"], "candidate") %> selected from <%= pluralize(@analysis.summary["conversations"], "conversation") %>. <%= @analysis.summary["represented_clusters"] %> of <%= @analysis.summary["clusters"] %> <%= @analysis.model? ? "proposed families" : "term clusters" %> represented. This measures this method's selection, not verified issue-family coverage.</p>
    <p>Taxonomy: <%= @taxonomy ? "expert revision #{@taxonomy.number}" : "unreviewed proposals" %>. <%= @analysis.model? ? "Possible documentation gaps and importance are model proposals; experts must check them." : "A possible documentation gap means no overlap between three cluster terms and the uploaded documents; experts must check it." %></p>
    <% if Current.require_membership!.can_write? && @analysis.summary["selected"].to_i.positive? %><%= button_to "Create selected scenarios", workspace_corpus_scenarios_path(Current.workspace, @corpus), params: { analysis_id: @analysis.id }, class: "button button-primary" %><% end %>
    <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="family-selection">
      <h2 id="family-selection">Review family selection</h2>
      <p>Find families with no selected candidate in this fixed analysis. The filter changes only this list, not selection, totals or scenario creation. It does not show which issues have tests elsewhere.</p>
      <%= form_with url: workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis), method: :get, class: "form-stack config-panel" do |form| %>
        <div class="field"><%= form.label :family_focus, "Family focus" %><%= select_tag :family_focus, options_for_select(@family_counts.map { |name, count| [ "#{name} (#{count})", name ] }, @family_focus), include_blank: @invalid_family_focus, aria: { invalid: @invalid_family_focus, describedby: @invalid_family_focus ? "family-focus-error" : nil } %></div>
        <% if @invalid_family_focus %><p id="family-focus-error" role="alert" class="inline-error">Choose a family focus from the list. <%= link_to "All families", workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis) %> clears the invalid filter.</p><% end %>
        <%= form.submit "Filter families", class: "button" %>
      <% end %>
      <% if !@invalid_family_focus && @clusters.empty? %>
        <% if @family_counts.fetch(@family_focus).zero? %>
          <p role="status">No families in this view. <%= link_to "All families", workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis) %> shows the complete selection.</p>
        <% else %>
          <p role="status">No families on this page. <%= link_to "First page", workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis, family_focus: @family_focus) %> keeps this focus.</p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </section>
    <% @clusters.each do |cluster| %>
      <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="cluster-<%= cluster.id %>">
        <h2 id="cluster-<%= cluster.id %>"><%= @taxonomy&.labels&.fetch(cluster.id.to_s, nil) || cluster.proposed_label %></h2>
        <p><%= pluralize(cluster.signals["count"], "conversation") %> · <%= @taxonomy&.labels&.key?(cluster.id.to_s) ? "Expert-reviewed label" : "Proposed label" %><% if cluster.signals["possible_documentation_gap"] %> · possible documentation gap<% end %></p>
        <% if @analysis.model? %><p><%= cluster.signals.fetch("proposal_reason") %></p><% end %>
        <% @examples.fetch(cluster).each do |member| %>
          <% item = @fixed_items.fetch(member.corpus_item_id) %>
          <details class="source-record"><summary><%= item.title %><%= member.selection_reason ? " — selected candidate" : "" %></summary>
            <p><%= member.signals.join(" · ") %></p><% if member.selection_reason %><p><%= member.selection_reason %></p><% end %>
            <%= link_to "Inspect source snapshot", source_evidence_path(item) %>
            <% if @analysis.model? %><h3>Membership quote</h3><pre class="evidence-text"><%= cluster.signals.fetch("evidence").find { |quote| quote.fetch("reference") == "corpus-item-#{member.corpus_item_id}" }.fetch("quote") %></pre><% end %>
            <pre class="evidence-text"><%= item.content %></pre>
          </details>
        <% end %>
        <p><% if @member_counts.fetch(cluster.id, 0) > 10 %>Showing 10 examples. <% end %><%= link_to "Explore all family records and source counts", workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_issue_cluster_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis, cluster) %></p>
        <% if Current.require_membership!.can_write? %>
          <%= form_with url: workspace_corpus_corpus_analysis_path(Current.workspace, @corpus, @analysis), method: :patch, class: "form-stack config-panel section-block" do |form| %>
            <%= form.hidden_field :cluster_id, value: cluster.id %>
            <div class="field"><%= form.label :label, "Expert issue label", for: "label-#{cluster.id}" %><%= form.text_field :label, id: "label-#{cluster.id}", value: @taxonomy&.labels&.fetch(cluster.id.to_s, nil) || cluster.proposed_label, required: true, maxlength: 120 %></div>
            <%= form.submit "Save expert label", class: "button" %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </section>
    <% end %>
    <%= render "shared/record_pagination", more: @more, page_number: @page %>
  <% end %>
</main>
